<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5 Results ‣ Fine-Tuning on Noisy Instructions: Effects on Generalization and Performance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Higher proportions of perturbed instructions appear to be beneficial in some contexts.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5 Results ‣ Fine-Tuning on Noisy Instructions: Effects on Generalization and Performance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Observed gains on standard unperturbed benchmarks from noisy fine-tuning.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 5 Results ‣ Fine-Tuning on Noisy Instructions: Effects on Generalization and Performance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">CoT remains more effective than direct prompting.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 5 Results ‣ Fine-Tuning on Noisy Instructions: Effects on Generalization and Performance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Instruction-tuning yields uneven gains across tasks.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
